## Step 3 — Notification Templates Seed
**Time: 45 minutes | Blocks: all SMS/email delivery**

The `notification-flush` job picks up `QUEUED` notifications and dispatches them. But `queueNotification()` silently drops any notification whose `templateSlug` doesn't match a DB record. If templates aren't seeded, the entire notification pipeline is silent.

**Audit every `queueNotification` call in the codebase to get all slugs:**

```bash
grep -rn "queueNotification\|templateSlug" apps/web/services/ apps/web/inngest/
```

**All slugs that must exist in the DB:**

```typescript
// packages/database/prisma/seed.ts — add/verify this block

const templates = [
  // Auth
  { slug: 'welcome',                channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'Welcome to Xkimm Xa Mali' },
  { slug: 'email-verification',     channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'Verify your email address' },
  { slug: 'password-reset',         channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'Reset your password' },
  { slug: 'account-activated',      channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },

  // Invite
  { slug: 'invite-created',         channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'invite-created-email',   channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'You have been invited to Xkimm Xa Mali' },

  // Payment lifecycle
  { slug: 'debit-morning-warning',  channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'debit-success',          channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'debit-success-email',    channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'Contribution received' },
  { slug: 'debit-declined',         channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'debit-declined-email',   channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'Contribution payment failed' },
  { slug: 'debit-pending',          channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },

  // Reminders
  { slug: 'overdue-reminder',       channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'overdue-reminder-email', channel: 'EMAIL', subject: 'Your contribution is overdue' },

  // Mandate
  { slug: 'mandate-cancelled',      channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'mandate-delayed',        channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },

  // Goals
  { slug: 'goal-activated',         channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },
  { slug: 'goal-achieved',          channel: 'SMS',   subject: null },

  // Admin broadcast
  { slug: 'broadcast',              channel: 'BOTH',  subject: null },
]

for (const template of templates) {
  await db.notificationTemplate.upsert({
    where: { slug: template.slug },
    create: template,
    update: {},   // never overwrite existing — admin can edit templates in DB
  })
}
```

The seed must be **idempotent** — `upsert` with `update: {}` means running it twice is safe. It only creates, never destroys.

**Add to your `package.json` seed script and run on every deploy in CI:**

```yaml
# .github/workflows/ci.yml — add after migrate deploy
- name: Seed database
  run: npm run db:seed
```

**Done when:** Every slug referenced in any `queueNotification` call has a corresponding `NotificationTemplate` record. Run `SELECT slug FROM notification_templates ORDER BY slug;` against your DB and compare manually.

