## Step 5 — Invite Flow End-to-End
**Time: 2 hours | Highest business priority**

This is the only way new members enter the system. It must work completely before anything else matters.

**Full flow with every file involved:**

```
Admin                          System                         Member
  │                              │                              │
  │── Creates invite ──────────► │                              │
  │   POST /api/v1/admin/        │── SMS: "XKM-XXXX-XXXX" ───► │
  │   invitations                │── Email: registration link ─► │
  │                              │                              │
  │                              │         ◄── Visits /invite/[token]
  │                              │◄── GET /api/v1/auth/         │
  │                              │    invitations/validate      │
  │                              │── Returns: name, email ─────► │
  │                              │   phone (pre-filled)         │
  │                              │                              │
  │                              │   ◄── Submits form ──────────│
  │                              │◄── POST /api/v1/auth/register│
  │                              │── Sends verify email ───────► │
  │                              │                              │
  │                              │      ◄── Clicks verify link ─│
  │                              │◄── GET /api/v1/auth/         │
  │                              │    verify-email?token=xxx    │
  │                              │── Status: PENDING ──────────► │
  │                              │                              │
  │◄── Sees PENDING member ──── │                              │
  │── Activates ───────────────► │                              │
  │   PATCH /api/v1/admin/       │── SMS: "Account active" ────► │
  │   members/[id]/status        │                              │
  │                              │      ◄── Logs in ────────────│
```

**File: `apps/web/app/invite/[token]/page.tsx`**

This page must:
1. Read the token from URL params
2. Call `GET /api/v1/auth/invitations/validate?code={token}` — server side
3. If valid: render the register form with email/phone pre-filled and read-only
4. If invalid/expired/used: render a clear error with a message to contact the admin

```typescript
// apps/web/app/invite/[token]/page.tsx
import { redirect } from 'next/navigation'

export default async function InvitePage({
  params,
}: {
  params: { token: string }
}) {
  const res = await fetch(
    `${process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_WEB_URL}/api/v1/auth/invitations/validate?code=${params.token}`,
    { cache: 'no-store' },
  )

  if (!res.ok) {
    const err = await res.json()
    return <InviteErrorView code={err.error?.code} />
  }

  const { data } = await res.json()
  return <RegisterForm invite={data} inviteCode={params.token} />
}
```

**The `RegisterForm` client component must:**
- Pre-fill `email` and `phone` as `readOnly` disabled fields (user cannot change them — they're bound to the invite)
- Collect: `firstName`, `lastName`, `password`, `confirmPassword`, `consentToPopia` checkbox
- Submit to `POST /api/v1/auth/register` with `inviteCode` in the body
- On success: redirect to `/auth/verify-email?sent=true`
- On error: display the error message (expired, already used, etc.)

**The `InviteErrorView` component must show:**

```
INV_001 (not found)  → "This invite link is invalid."
INV_002 (used)       → "This invite link has already been used. If you have an account, log in."
INV_003 (revoked)    → "This invite link has been revoked. Contact the group admin."
INV_004 (expired)    → "This invite link has expired. Ask the admin to resend your invite."
```

**File: `apps/web/app/(auth)/verify-email/page.tsx`**

After registration, member lands here. Two states:
1. `?sent=true` — show "Check your email" message
2. `?token=xxx` — this is the link from the email, calls `GET /api/v1/auth/verify-email?token=xxx`, redirects to `/auth/login?verified=true`

**File: `apps/web/app/(auth)/login/page.tsx`**

The `LoginForm` must handle:
- `?verified=true` query param → show "Email verified. You can now log in."
- After successful login if user status is `PENDING` → show "Your account is pending admin approval. You'll receive an SMS when it's activated."
- Normal login → redirect to `/dashboard`

**Done when:** You can complete the full flow manually from a fresh invite with a real email and phone number, end-to-end, without touching the database directly.

